00:09:17,312 --> 00:09:19,448
increasingly show up where it hurts.

288
00:09:19,628 --> 00:09:22,327
The safe assumption today is simple:

289
00:09:22,327 --> 00:09:23,827
treat every buy now,

290
00:09:23,827 --> 00:09:25,927
pay later plan as real debt,

291
00:09:25,927 --> 00:09:26,977
because it is.

292
00:09:27,327 --> 00:09:30,473
The phantom debt problem also affects households.

293
00:09:30,653 --> 00:09:32,516
Couples can be surprised to find their

294
00:09:32,516 --> 00:09:34,182
partner has several plans running.

295
00:09:34,362 --> 00:09:36,539
Parents may not realize a young adult

296
00:09:36,539 --> 00:09:37,892
child is juggling them.

297
00:09:38,072 --> 00:09:40,677
Because these loans are small and live

298
00:09:40,677 --> 00:09:43,009
inside apps, they're easy to hide,

299
00:09:43,009 --> 00:09:44,655
even without meaning to.

300
00:09:45,005 --> 00:09:46,107
Number six.

301
00:09:46,287 --> 00:09:47,588
Who uses it most.

302
00:09:47,938 --> 00:09:49,869
The CFPB found that buy now,

303
00:09:49,869 --> 00:09:51,594
pay later borrowers were,

304
00:09:51,594 --> 00:09:54,077
on average, more likely to have high

305
00:09:54,077 --> 00:09:55,526
levels of other debt,

306
00:09:55,526 --> 00:09:56,767
like credit cards,

307
00:09:56,767 --> 00:09:59,251
and more likely to carry balances on

308
00:09:59,251 --> 00:10:01,941
those cards, than people who didn't use

309
00:10:01,941 --> 00:10:02,148
it.

310
00:10:02,328 --> 00:10:03,406
Many were younger,

311
00:10:03,406 --> 00:10:05,382
and many had lower credit scores.

312
00:10:05,562 --> 00:10:06,502
In other words,

313
00:10:06,502 --> 00:10:08,695
the product is often used by people

314
00:10:08,695 --> 00:10:10,826
who already have the least room in

315
00:10:10,826 --> 00:10:11,703
their budgets.

316
00:10:12,054 --> 00:10:13,929
That doesn't mean everyone who uses it

317
00:10:13,929 --> 00:10:14,619
is in trouble.

318
00:10:14,799 --> 00:10:17,310
Plenty of people use it for convenience

319
00:10:17,310 --> 00:10:19,049
and pay everything on time.

320
00:10:19,229 --> 00:10:20,968
But it does mean that for a

321
00:10:20,968 --> 00:10:22,320
large group of users,

322
00:10:22,320 --> 00:10:24,961
buy now, pay later isn't replacing credit

323
00:10:24,961 --> 00:10:25,347
cards.

324
00:10:25,527 --> 00:10:26,467
It's adding to them.

325
00:10:26,647 --> 00:10:29,051
More debt, spread across more places.

326
00:10:29,401 --> 00:10:32,410
And the Federal Reserve's household survey has

327
00:10:32,410 --> 00:10:34,765
found that a meaningful share of buy

328
00:10:34,765 --> 00:10:37,448
now, pay later users reported paying late

329
00:10:37,448 --> 00:10:38,363
at least once.

330
00:10:38,543 --> 00:10:41,029
When people who already carry other debts

331
00:10:41,029 --> 00:10:42,787
start missing small payments,

332
00:10:42,787 --> 00:10:44,545
it's often a sign of a bigger

333
00:10:44,545 --> 00:10:46,485
squeeze in the household budget.

334
00:10:46,665 --> 00:10:48,978
The small late payment is the warning

335
00:10:48,978 --> 00:10:50,728
light, not the real problem.

336
00:10:51,079 --> 00:10:52,588
Regulators have noticed.

337
00:10:52,768 --> 00:10:55,354
The CFPB has published several reports on

338
00:10:55,354 --> 00:10:56,553
buy now, pay later,

339
00:10:56,553 --> 00:10:58,445
and the rules that apply to it

340
00:10:58,445 --> 00:11:00,905
have been debated and changed more than

341
00:11:00,905 --> 00:11:02,230
once in recent years.

342
00:11:02,410 --> 00:11:04,982
Other countries have also moved to regulate

343
00:11:04,982 --> 00:11:05,939
it more closely.

344
00:11:06,119 --> 00:11:08,597
For you, the practical lesson is that

345
00:11:08,597 --> 00:11:11,475
protections can vary by provider and change

346
00:11:11,475 --> 00:11:12,145
over time.

347
00:11:12,325 --> 00:11:13,797
Don't assume a buy now,

348
00:11:13,797 --> 00:11:15,909
pay later loan gives you the same

349
00:11:15,909 --> 00:11:17,445
rights as a credit card.

350
00:11:17,625 --> 00:11:20,144
Read the dispute and refund terms.

351
00:11:20,495 --> 00:11:22,816
So the numbers show a product that's

352
00:11:22,816 --> 00:11:25,330
huge, growing, and used most heavily by

353
00:11:25,330 --> 00:11:27,135
people with the least slack.

354
00:11:27,315 --> 00:11:29,289
Now let's look at why it changes

355
00:11:29,289 --> 00:11:30,090
how we spend.

356
00:11:30,441 --> 00:11:31,451
Angle two.

357
00:11:31,631 --> 00:11:32,757
The psychology.

358
00:11:32,937 --> 00:11:35,550
Seven reasons splitting a price makes us

359
00:11:35,550 --> 00:11:36,269
spend more.

360
00:11:36,619 --> 00:11:37,896
Reason number seven.

361
00:11:38,076 --> 00:11:39,608
The smaller number wins.

362
00:11:39,959 --> 00:11:42,148
When a two hundred dollar jacket is

363
00:11:42,148 --> 00:11:44,650
shown as four payments of fifty dollars,

364
00:11:44,650 --> 00:11:46,402
your brain anchors on fifty.

365
00:11:46,582 --> 00:11:48,347
Fifty feels affordable.

366
00:11:48,527 --> 00:11:50,233
Two hundred might make you pause.

367
00:11:50,413 --> 00:11:52,329
It's the same jacket and the same

368
00:11:52,329 --> 00:11:54,361
total, but the number you see first

369
00:11:54,361 --> 00:11:55,580
changes the decision.

370
00:11:55,760 --> 00:11:57,931
Marketers have known this for a long

371
00:11:57,931 --> 00:11:58,233
time.

372
00:11:58,413 --> 00:12:00,879
It's the same reason gym memberships are

373
00:12:00,879 --> 00:12:02,974
priced per day and cars are priced

374
00:12:02,974 --> 00:12:03,591
per month.

375
00:12:03,941 --> 00:12:06,982
Researchers who study pricing call this partitioning.

376
00:12:07,162 --> 00:12:09,370
When a price is broken into parts,

377
00:12:09,370 --> 00:12:11,772
people often underestimate the total.

378
00:12:11,952 --> 00:12:12,841
With buy now,

379
00:12:12,841 --> 00:12:15,510
pay later, the partition is right there

380
00:12:15,510 --> 00:12:16,468
on the button.

381
00:12:16,648 --> 00:12:19,067
Pay four interest free payments of fifty

382
00:12:19,067 --> 00:12:19,550
dollars.

383
00:12:19,730 --> 00:12:21,940
The two hundred is technically shown,

384
00:12:21,940 --> 00:12:23,434
but it's not what sticks.

385
00:12:23,784 --> 00:12:26,311
Try this: before using a split payment,

386
00:12:26,311 --> 00:12:28,126
say the full price out loud.

387
00:12:28,306 --> 00:12:30,047
Not four payments of fifty.

388
00:12:30,227 --> 00:12:31,504
Two hundred dollars.

389
00:12:31,684 --> 00:12:33,420
Then ask whether you'd buy it at

390
00:12:33,420 --> 00:12:34,668
that price, paid today.

391
00:12:34,848 --> 00:12:36,368
If the answer is yes,

392
00:12:36,368 --> 00:12:38,540
the split is just convenience.

393
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:40,062
If the answer is no,

394
00:12:40,062 --> 00:12:42,342
the split is doing the persuading.

395
00:12:42,693 --> 00:12:43,807
Reason number eight.

396
00:12:43,987 --> 00:12:45,438
It doesn't feel like debt.

397
00:12:45,789 --> 00:12:47,727
Most people know credit cards are debt.

398
00:12:47,907 --> 00:12:48,736
But buy now,

399
00:12:48,736 --> 00:12:50,531
pay later feels different.

400
00:12:50,711 --> 00:12:52,195
There's no plastic card,

401
00:12:52,195 --> 00:12:53,864
often no hard credit check,

402
00:12:53,864 --> 00:12:55,657
and the language is friendly.

403
00:12:55,837 --> 00:12:58,403
Plans, installments, splitting.

404
00:12:58,583 --> 00:13:00,952
Many users don't think of themselves as

405
00:13:00,952 --> 00:13:01,985
borrowers at all.

406
00:13:02,165 --> 00:13:03,975
And if you don't think it's debt,

407
00:13:03,975 --> 00:13:05,731
you don't treat it with the same

408
00:13:05,731 --> 00:13:06,170
caution.

409
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:08,348
But legally and practically,

410
00:13:08,348 --> 00:13:09,132
it's a loan.

411
00:13:09,312 --> 00:13:11,495
You receive something now and promise to

412
00:13:11,495 --> 00:13:12,423
pay for it later.

413
00:13:12,603 --> 00:13:13,709
If you don't pay,

414
00:13:13,709 --> 00:13:15,206
there are consequences:

415
00:13:15,206 --> 00:13:18,199
fees, collections, and possibly credit damage.

416
00:13:18,379 --> 00:13:21,038
The friendly language doesn't change the obligation.

417
00:13:21,218 --> 00:13:23,287
It just makes it easier to say

418
00:13:23,287 --> 00:13:23,563
yes.

419
00:13:23,914 --> 00:13:25,980
Try this: rename it in your head.

420
00:13:26,160 --> 00:13:27,993
Every time you see the button,

421
00:13:27,993 --> 00:13:29,643
read it as take out a loan.

422
00:13:29,823 --> 00:13:31,890
Take out a loan for these headphones.

423
00:13:32,070 --> 00:13:33,788
Take out a loan for this dinner.

424
00:13:33,968 --> 00:13:35,236
It sounds dramatic,

425
00:13:35,236 --> 00:13:36,905
but it's simply accurate.

426
00:13:37,085 --> 00:13:38,948
And it brings back the caution that

427
00:13:38,948 --> 00:13:40,545
the friendly language removes.

428
00:13:40,895 --> 00:13:42,148
Reason number nine.

429
00:13:42,328 --> 00:13:43,455
Less pain of paying.

430
00:13:43,805 --> 00:13:44,942
Paying hurts a little.

431
00:13:45,122 --> 00:13:47,375
That small pain is actually useful.

432
00:13:47,555 --> 00:13:48,460
It makes you think.

433
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:51,617
Researchers have shown that people often spend

434
00:13:51,617 --> 00:13:53,624
more when the pain of paying is

435
00:13:53,624 --> 00:13:56,277
reduced, for example by paying with cards

436
00:13:56,277 --> 00:13:57,313
instead of cash.

437
00:13:57,493 --> 00:13:59,683
Buy now, pay later reduces it even

438
00:13:59,683 --> 00:14:00,198
further.

439
00:14:00,378 --> 00:14:01,962
You pay only a quarter today,

440
00:14:01,962 --> 00:14:04,202
and the rest happens automatically later,

441
00:14:04,202 --> 00:14:06,333
when the excitement of buying has moved

442
00:14:06,333 --> 00:14:06,497
on.

443
00:14:06,847 --> 00:14:09,140
This also separates the joy from the

444
00:14:09,140 --> 00:14:09,459
cost.

445
00:14:09,639 --> 00:14:11,137
You enjoy the purchase now.

446
00:14:11,317 --> 00:14:13,054
The payments arrive in two,

447
00:14:13,054 --> 00:14:14,276
four and six weeks,

448
00:14:14,276 --> 00:14:16,979
when you might be enjoying something else,

449
00:14:16,979 --> 00:14:18,909
also bought with a split plan.

450
00:14:19,089 --> 00:14:21,763
The cost and the pleasure never meet,

451
00:14:21,763 --> 00:14:23,931
so the cost never feels as big

452
00:14:23,931 --> 00:14:24,581
as it is.

453
00:14:24,931 --> 00:14:26,601
Try this: if you do use a

454
00:14:26,601 --> 00:14:29,340
split plan, put every future payment date

455
00:14:29,340 --> 00:14:31,746
in your calendar with the item name.

456
00:14:31,926 --> 00:14:33,604
Payment three of four,

457
00:14:33,604 --> 00:14:35,664
jacket, forty five dollars.

458
00:14:35,844 --> 00:14:37,331
When the reminder appears,

459
00:14:37,331 --> 00:14:39,675
you reconnect the cost with the purchase.

460
00:14:39,855 --> 00:14:41,039
It's a small habit,

461
00:14:41,039 --> 00:14:43,220
and it makes the real price visible

462
00:14:43,220 --> 00:14:43,594
again.

463
00:14:43,944 --> 00:14:45,128
Reason number ten.

464
00:14:45,308 --> 00:14:46,225
Bigger carts.

465
00:14:46,575 --> 00:14:48,123
When the total is split,

466
00:14:48,123 --> 00:14:50,574
a more expensive option starts to look

467
00:14:50,574 --> 00:14:51,219
reachable.

468
00:14:51,399 --> 00:14:53,561
The one hundred fifty dollar shoes feel

469
00:14:53,561 --> 00:14:55,224
like they cost the same as the

470
00:14:55,224 --> 00:14:56,555
one hundred dollar ones,

471
00:14:56,555 --> 00:14:58,606
because the split payments are only a

472
00:14:58,606 --> 00:14:59,549
little different.

473
00:14:59,729 --> 00:15:02,459
Merchants report larger average orders when split

474
00:15:02,459 --> 00:15:03,630
payments are offered.

475
00:15:03,810 --> 00:15:05,630
That's one of the main reasons they

476
00:15:05,630 --> 00:15:06,306
pay the fees.

477
00:15:06,656 --> 00:15:08,646
Try this: when you see a split

478
00:15:08,646 --> 00:15:11,432
payment option, decide what you were going

479
00:15:11,432 --> 00:15:13,622
to buy before you saw the button.

480
00:15:13,802 --> 00:15:15,728
Then stick to that item and that

481
00:15:15,728 --> 00:15:16,089
price.

482
00:15:16,269 --> 00:15:18,068
The button can change how you pay.

483
00:15:18,248 --> 00:15:19,885
It shouldn't change what you buy.

484
00:15:20,236 --> 00:15:23,347
This works for subscriptions and memberships too.

485
00:15:23,527 --> 00:15:25,776
Many offers now show a monthly price

486
00:15:25,776 --> 00:15:27,650
for things you used to pay for

487
00:15:27,650 --> 00:15:27,962
once.

488
00:15:28,142 --> 00:15:30,661
The smaller number always looks friendlier.

489
00:15:30,841 --> 00:15:33,107
Always convert it back to the yearly

490
00:15:33,107 --> 00:15:34,051
or total price,

491
00:15:34,051 --> 00:15:35,625
and decide based on that.

492
00:15:35,975 --> 00:15:37,217
Reason number eleven.

493
00:15:37,397 --> 00:15:38,593
Instant approval.

494
00:15:38,943 --> 00:15:40,812
Traditional loans have friction.

495
00:15:40,992 --> 00:15:43,859
Applications, waiting, maybe a call from the

496
00:15:43,859 --> 00:15:44,185
bank.

497
00:15:44,365 --> 00:15:46,478
That friction gives you time to reconsider.

498
00:15:46,658 --> 00:15:49,292
Buy now, pay later approval often takes

499
00:15:49,292 --> 00:15:51,116
seconds, right at checkout.

500
00:15:51,296 --> 00:15:53,511
There's no pause between I want this

501
00:15:53,511 --> 00:15:54,372
and it's mine.

502
00:15:54,552 --> 00:15:56,637
Speed is great for convenience,

503
00:15:56,637 --> 00:15:59,057
and dangerous for impulse purchases.

504
00:15:59,407 --> 00:16:01,334
Late night shopping makes it worse.

505
00:16:01,514 --> 00:16:04,090
Tired, scrolling, a little bored,

506
00:16:04,090 --> 00:16:06,197
and one tap away from a new

507
00:16:06,197 --> 00:16:06,587
plan.

508
00:16:06,767 --> 00:16:09,724
Many impulse purchases happen exactly in those

509
00:16:09,724 --> 00:16:10,239
moments.

510
00:16:10,419 --> 00:16:12,799
Try this: create a personal rule.

511
00:16:12,979 --> 00:16:15,730
No split payment purchases after nine p.

512
00:16:15,910 --> 00:16:16,131
m.

513
00:16:16,311 --> 00:16:17,746
If you still want it in the

514
00:16:17,746 --> 00:16:18,703
morning, go ahead.

515
00:16:19,053 --> 00:16:21,038
You can also add your own friction.

516
00:16:21,218 --> 00:16:23,069
Use a separate debit card with a

517
00:16:23,069 --> 00:16:25,268
set weekly amount for online shopping,

518
00:16:25,268 --> 00:16:27,524
so you physically can't spend more than

519
00:16:27,524 --> 00:16:28,219
you planned.

520
00:16:28,399 --> 00:16:30,515
Or log out of shopping apps after

521
00:16:30,515 --> 00:16:31,092
each use.

522
00:16:31,272 --> 00:16:33,082
The few extra seconds it takes to

523
00:16:33,082 --> 00:16:34,838
log back in are often enough for

524
00:16:34,838 --> 00:16:36,648
your better judgment to catch up.

525
00:16:36,998 --> 00:16:38,298
Reason number twelve.

526
00:16:38,478 --> 00:16:39,639
It's normal now.

527
00:16:39,989 --> 00:16:42,160
Social media is full of hauls and

528
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:45,188
outfits, sometimes bought with split payments,

529
00:16:45,188 --> 00:16:47,360
and the option appears on so many

530
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:49,597
stores that it starts to feel like

531
00:16:49,597 --> 00:16:51,111
the default way to pay.

532
00:16:51,291 --> 00:16:53,359
When something is everywhere,

533
00:16:53,359 --> 00:16:54,786
we assume it's safe.

534
00:16:54,966 --> 00:16:56,956
When friends use it casually,

535
00:16:56,956 --> 00:16:58,878
it feels responsible enough.

536
00:16:59,228 --> 00:17:01,489
But being normal doesn't make something right

537
00:17:01,489 --> 00:17:02,293
for your budget.

538
00:17:02,473 --> 00:17:05,639
Remember, the CFPB found many users already

539
00:17:05,639 --> 00:17:07,848
had high levels of other debt.

540
00:17:08,028 --> 00:17:10,036
Normal can mean that many people are

541
00:17:10,036 --> 00:17:10,594
stretched.

542
00:17:10,774 --> 00:17:13,243
Try this: follow your own numbers,

543
00:17:13,243 --> 00:17:14,187
not the feed.

544
00:17:14,367 --> 00:17:17,098
If your monthly split payments ever exceed

545
00:17:17,098 --> 00:17:18,788
what you'd put in savings,

546
00:17:18,788 --> 00:17:19,894
something is off.

547
00:17:20,244 --> 00:17:23,138
It's also worth remembering that some creators

548
00:17:23,138 --> 00:17:25,655
earn commissions on what they recommend,

549
00:17:25,655 --> 00:17:28,235
and promoted posts don't always look like

550
00:17:28,235 --> 00:17:28,487
ads.

551
00:17:28,667 --> 00:17:29,644
That's not wrong,

552
00:17:29,644 --> 00:17:31,656
but it means the person telling you

553
00:17:31,656 --> 00:17:33,438
to buy may benefit when you do.

554
00:17:33,618 --> 00:17:34,768
Enjoy the content.

555
00:17:34,948 --> 00:17:36,376
Make your own decisions.

556
00:17:36,726 --> 00:17:38,293
Reason number thirteen.

557
00:17:38,473 --> 00:17:39,587
Losing track.

558
00:17:39,938 --> 00:17:41,737
When debts live in one place,

559
00:17:41,737 --> 00:17:43,971
like a single credit card statement,

560
00:17:43,971 --> 00:17:45,336
you can see the total.

561
00:17:45,516 --> 00:17:48,054
Buy now, pay later spreads debt across

562
00:17:48,054 --> 00:17:50,926
different apps, each with its own schedule.

563
00:17:51,106 --> 00:17:53,696
Your brain counts each one as small.

564
00:17:53,876 --> 00:17:55,362
Nobody adds them up.

565
00:17:55,542 --> 00:17:58,024
And if payments come out automatically from

566
00:17:58,024 --> 00:17:58,947
your debit card,

567
00:17:58,947 --> 00:18:00,910
they can pull money you needed for

568
00:18:00,910 --> 00:18:01,718
rent or bills.

569
00:18:02,068 --> 00:18:04,477
This can trigger overdraft fees at your

570
00:18:04,477 --> 00:18:06,269
bank, on top of any late fees

571
00:18:06,269 --> 00:18:07,257
from the lender.

572
00:18:07,437 --> 00:18:09,562
Two fees for one small payment.

573
00:18:09,742 --> 00:18:11,264
Try this: once a week,

574
00:18:11,264 --> 00:18:12,578
open every buy now,

575
00:18:12,578 --> 00:18:14,722
pay later app you use and write

576
00:18:14,722 --> 00:18:16,936
down the total you owe and every

577
00:18:16,936 --> 00:18:18,458
due date in one place,

578
00:18:18,458 --> 00:18:20,187
a note on your phone or a

579
00:18:20,187 --> 00:18:21,294
simple calendar.

580
00:18:21,474 --> 00:18:22,194
One total.

581
00:18:22,374 --> 00:18:23,279
One list.

582
00:18:23,630 --> 00:18:25,267
When you write the total down,

583
00:18:25,267 --> 00:18:27,287
compare it with your monthly savings.

584
00:18:27,467 --> 00:18:29,590
If you owe more in split payments

585
00:18:29,590 --> 00:18:31,198
than you save each month,

586
00:18:31,198 --> 00:18:33,385
that's a clear signal to pause new

587
00:18:33,385 --> 00:18:35,315
plans until the list is empty.

588
00:18:35,495 --> 00:18:37,778
Most people who do this exercise once

589
00:18:37,778 --> 00:18:39,690
say it changes how they use the

590
00:18:39,690 --> 00:18:40,615
button forever.

591
00:18:40,965 --> 00:18:42,272
Before the playbook,

592
00:18:42,272 --> 00:18:43,449
a quick self test.

593
00:18:43,629 --> 00:18:43,780
One.

594
00:18:43,960 --> 00:18:45,639
Do you have more than one buy

595
00:18:45,639 --> 00:18:47,838
now, pay later plan running right now?

596
00:18:48,018 --> 00:18:48,296
Two.

597
00:18:48,476 --> 00:18:50,250
Have you used it for food,

598
00:18:50,250 --> 00:18:52,911
groceries or takeout in the last month?

599
00:18:53,091 --> 00:18:53,556
Three.

600
00:18:53,736 --> 00:18:55,303
Do you know the total you owe

601
00:18:55,303 --> 00:18:56,168
across all apps,

602
00:18:56,168 --> 00:18:57,033
without looking?

603
00:18:57,383 --> 00:18:57,917
Four.

604
00:18:58,097 --> 00:19:00,284
Have you ever moved money between accounts

605
00:19:00,284 --> 00:19:01,533
to cover an installment?

606
00:19:01,713 --> 00:19:02,120
Five.

607
00:19:02,300 --> 00:19:03,887
Have you paid a late fee or

608
00:19:03,887 --> 00:19:05,945
an overdraft fee because of a plan?

609
00:19:06,125 --> 00:19:06,961
And six.

610
00:19:07,141 --> 00:19:08,828
Would you have bought the last thing

611
00:19:08,828 --> 00:19:10,093
you split if you had to pay

612
00:19:10,093 --> 00:19:11,077
the full price today?

613
00:19:11,257 --> 00:19:13,363
If you answered yes to the first

614
00:19:13,363 --> 00:19:15,206
five, or no to the last one,

615
00:19:15,206 --> 00:19:16,194
more than once,

616
00:19:16,194 --> 00:19:18,629
the playbook that follows is for you.

617
00:19:18,979 --> 00:19:20,047
Quick pause.

618
00:19:20,227 --> 00:19:22,003
If you just counted how many plans

619
00:19:22,003 --> 00:19:23,414
you have running right now,

620
00:19:23,414 --> 00:19:24,302
you're not alone.

621
00:19:24,482 --> 00:19:26,495
Subscribe to the channel if this is

622
00:19:26,495 --> 00:19:26,955
helping.

623
00:19:27,135 --> 00:19:28,831
It's free, and it helps me keep

624
00:19:28,831 --> 00:19:30,362
making these videos for you.

625
00:19:30,542 --> 00:19:31,680
Now the playbook.

626
00:19:32,030 --> 00:19:33,017
Angle three.

627
00:19:33,197 --> 00:19:33,986
The playbook.

628
00:19:34,166 --> 00:19:35,063
When buy now,

629
00:19:35,063 --> 00:19:36,305
pay later is fine,

630
00:19:36,305 --> 00:19:37,685
when it's dangerous,

631
00:19:37,685 --> 00:19:38,996
and how to get out.

632
00:19:39,346 --> 00:19:41,389
Rule one, the golden rule.

633
00:19:41,569 --> 00:19:42,605
Only use buy now,

634
00:19:42,605 --> 00:19:44,860
pay later for something you could pay

635
00:19:44,860 --> 00:19:45,958
for in full today,

636
00:19:45,958 --> 00:19:47,664
with money you already have.

637
00:19:47,844 --> 00:19:49,300
If you can afford it now,

638
00:19:49,300 --> 00:19:51,455
splitting it is just a timing choice.

639
00:19:51,635 --> 00:19:52,412
If you can't,

640
00:19:52,412 --> 00:19:53,967
the plan is a loan you may

641
00:19:53,967 --> 00:19:55,222
not be able to repay.

642
00:19:55,402 --> 00:19:57,604
This one rule eliminates most of the

643
00:19:57,604 --> 00:19:57,910
risk.

644
00:19:58,260 --> 00:19:59,165
Rule two.

645
00:19:59,345 --> 00:20:00,529
One plan at a time.

646
00:20:00,709 --> 00:20:01,569
Never stack.

647
00:20:01,749 --> 00:20:03,229
If you have a plan running,

648
00:20:03,229 --> 00:20:05,092
finish it before starting another.

649
00:20:05,272 --> 00:20:07,121
This keeps the total visible and the

650
00:20:07,121 --> 00:20:07,943
schedule simple.

651
00:20:08,123 --> 00:20:08,982
Rule three.

652
00:20:09,162 --> 00:20:10,810
Never for consumables.

653
00:20:10,990 --> 00:20:12,800
Food, takeout, groceries,

654
00:20:12,800 --> 00:20:15,623
and everyday items are gone long before

655
00:20:15,623 --> 00:20:16,853
the payments end.

656
00:20:17,033 --> 00:20:18,981
Paying later for a meal you ate

657
00:20:18,981 --> 00:20:20,866
weeks ago is a sign the budget

658
00:20:20,866 --> 00:20:23,129
needs attention, not a payment plan.

659
00:20:23,479 --> 00:20:24,280
Rule four.

660
00:20:24,460 --> 00:20:25,911
Know the type of plan.

661
00:20:26,091 --> 00:20:27,932
Pay in four with no interest is

662
00:20:27,932 --> 00:20:30,663
very different from a twelve month installment

663
00:20:30,663 --> 00:20:31,792
loan with interest.

664
00:20:31,972 --> 00:20:34,108
Read the APR before you tap.

665
00:20:34,288 --> 00:20:35,298
Rule five.

666
00:20:35,478 --> 00:20:36,650
Pay from the right account.

667
00:20:36,830 --> 00:20:38,872
If payments come from a debit card,

668
00:20:38,872 --> 00:20:40,796
make sure the money will be there

669
00:20:40,796 --> 00:20:41,788
on each due date.

670
00:20:41,968 --> 00:20:44,743
Many people prefer to set reminders and

671
00:20:44,743 --> 00:20:46,949
pay manually, or pay off early.

672
00:20:47,299 --> 00:20:48,320
Rule six.

673
00:20:48,500 --> 00:20:49,673
Turn off the button.

674
00:20:49,853 --> 00:20:52,168
Some apps and browsers let you hide

675
00:20:52,168 --> 00:20:53,954
or disable payment options,

676
00:20:53,954 --> 00:20:56,204
and you can remove saved accounts.

677
00:20:56,384 --> 00:20:58,264
Less temptation at checkout.

678
00:20:58,444 --> 00:20:59,292
Rule seven.

679
00:20:59,472 --> 00:21:00,703
Keep one list.

680
00:21:00,883 --> 00:21:02,827
Every plan, every due date,

681
00:21:02,827 --> 00:21:04,772
every amount, in one place.

682
00:21:04,952 --> 00:21:06,322
Review it weekly.

683
00:21:06,672 --> 00:21:07,450
Rule eight.

684
00:21:07,630 --> 00:21:08,503
If you use it,

685
00:21:08,503 --> 00:21:10,625
use it for planned purchases only.

686
00:21:10,805 --> 00:21:12,452
Something you budgeted for,

687
00:21:12,452 --> 00:21:14,343
at a price you decided ahead of

688
00:21:14,343 --> 00:21:14,648
time.

689
00:21:14,828 --> 00:21:16,999
A new fridge when the old one

690
00:21:16,999 --> 00:21:19,695
dies, paid in four with no interest,

691
00:21:19,695 --> 00:21:22,166
from money you already set aside,

692
00:21:22,166 --> 00:21:23,663
is a reasonable use.

693
00:21:23,843 --> 00:21:26,177
An impulse outfit at midnight is not.

694
00:21:26,527 --> 00:21:28,408
The golden rule of buy now,

695
00:21:28,408 --> 00:21:29,104
pay later.

696
00:21:29,284 --> 00:21:30,972
Only split what you could pay for

697
00:21:30,972 --> 00:21:31,687
in full today.

698
00:21:32,038 --> 00:21:34,872
And if you're already juggling several plans,

699
00:21:34,872 --> 00:21:36,258
here's how to get out,

700
00:21:36,258 --> 00:21:37,076
step by step.

701
00:21:37,427 --> 00:21:38,205
Step one.

702
00:21:38,385 --> 00:21:39,279
Stop adding.

703
00:21:39,459 --> 00:21:41,710
No new plans until all current ones

704
00:21:41,710 --> 00:21:42,547
are finished.

705
00:21:42,727 --> 00:21:45,446
Remove saved payment methods from your shopping

706
00:21:45,446 --> 00:21:46,198
apps for now.

707
00:21:46,378 --> 00:21:47,319
Step two.

708
00:21:47,499 --> 00:21:48,532
Make the list.

709
00:21:48,712 --> 00:21:49,735
Open every app,

710
00:21:49,735 --> 00:21:52,533
write every remaining payment and date in

711
00:21:52,533 --> 00:21:54,238
one place, and add it up.

712
00:21:54,418 --> 00:21:56,609
Knowing the real total is uncomfortable,

713
00:21:56,609 --> 00:21:58,087
but it's the turning point.

714
00:21:58,437 --> 00:21:59,331
Step three.

715
00:21:59,511 --> 00:22:00,985
Protect the essentials.

716
00:22:01,165 --> 00:22:05,507
Rent, utilities, food and transportation come first.

717
00:22:05,687 --> 00:22:08,183
If a payment date clashes with rent,

718
00:22:08,183 --> 00:22:10,817
contact the lender before the due date

719
00:22:10,817 --> 00:22:12,688
and ask about rescheduling.

720
00:22:12,868 --> 00:22:15,281
Many providers let you move a payment

721
00:22:15,281 --> 00:22:17,303
date or offer hardship options.

722
00:22:17,483 --> 00:22:19,677
Ask early, not after you've missed it.

723
00:22:20,028 --> 00:22:21,096
Step four.

724
00:22:21,276 --> 00:22:23,320
Clear the smallest plans first,

725
00:22:23,320 --> 00:22:24,968
if the costs are similar.

726
00:22:25,148 --> 00:22:27,779
Finishing a plan entirely reduces the number

727
00:22:27,779 --> 00:22:28,557
of due dates,

728
00:22:28,557 --> 00:22:30,590
which lowers your risk of a missed

729
00:22:30,590 --> 00:22:31,069
payment.

730
00:22:31,249 --> 00:22:33,417
Any plan that charges interest should move

731
00:22:33,417 --> 00:22:34,604
to the top of the list.

732
00:22:34,784 --> 00:22:35,829
Step five.

733
00:22:36,009 --> 00:22:37,456
Build a small cushion,

734
00:22:37,456 --> 00:22:39,692
even two or three hundred dollars,

735
00:22:39,692 --> 00:22:41,993
so a surprise doesn't push you back

736
00:22:41,993 --> 00:22:43,834
to splitting everyday costs.

737
00:22:44,184 --> 00:22:45,449
And step six.

738
00:22:45,629 --> 00:22:47,080
Look at the bigger picture.

739
00:22:47,260 --> 00:22:49,880
If you've been using split payments to

740
00:22:49,880 --> 00:22:51,466
cover regular expenses,

741
00:22:51,466 --> 00:22:53,742
the real issue is the gap between

742
00:22:53,742 --> 00:22:55,120
income and spending.

743
00:22:55,300 --> 00:22:57,367
Use the same tools from my video

744
00:22:57,367 --> 00:22:59,305
on why most people stay broke:

745
00:22:59,305 --> 00:23:00,726
find your real number,

746
00:23:00,726 --> 00:23:01,630
cut the leaks,

747
00:23:01,630 --> 00:23:03,439
and build a starter cushion.

748
00:23:03,619 --> 00:23:05,001
The plans are a symptom.

749
00:23:05,181 --> 00:23:06,469
The budget is the cure.

750
00:23:06,819 --> 00:23:08,953
Let's walk through one month in the

751
00:23:08,953 --> 00:23:11,148
life of someone using several plans,

752
00:23:11,148 --> 00:23:12,917
so you can see how quickly it

753
00:23:12,917 --> 00:23:13,344
builds.

754
00:23:13,694 --> 00:23:14,251
Day one.

755
00:23:14,431 --> 00:23:17,832
Paycheck arrives, two thousand dollars after taxes

756
00:23:17,832 --> 00:23:18,785
for two weeks.

757
00:23:18,965 --> 00:23:19,890
Rent comes out,

758
00:23:19,890 --> 00:23:21,988
plus the car payment and the phone

759
00:23:21,988 --> 00:23:22,297
bill.

760
00:23:22,477 --> 00:23:24,683
About seven hundred dollars is left for

761
00:23:24,683 --> 00:23:25,588
everything else.

762
00:23:25,768 --> 00:23:27,022
Day three.

763
00:23:27,202 --> 00:23:29,929
A forty dollar installment for sneakers bought

764
00:23:29,929 --> 00:23:30,581
last month.

765
00:23:30,761 --> 00:23:31,666
Day five.

766
00:23:31,846 --> 00:23:34,609
A sixty dollar installment for a jacket.

767
00:23:34,789 --> 00:23:35,556
Day seven.

768
00:23:35,736 --> 00:23:38,965
A thirty dollar installment for groceries split

769
00:23:38,965 --> 00:23:39,927
two weeks ago.

770
00:23:40,277 --> 00:23:40,973
Day ten.

771
00:23:41,153 --> 00:23:43,540
A ninety dollar installment for a new

772
00:23:43,540 --> 00:23:45,797
phone accessory bundle and earbuds.

773
00:23:45,977 --> 00:23:46,813
Day twelve.

774
00:23:46,993 --> 00:23:49,901
A seventy five dollar installment for concert

775
00:23:49,901 --> 00:23:50,418
tickets.

776
00:23:50,598 --> 00:23:52,386
Nothing seems big on its own.

777
00:23:52,566 --> 00:23:54,310
But by the end of two weeks,

778
00:23:54,310 --> 00:23:56,739
close to three hundred dollars has gone

779
00:23:56,739 --> 00:23:57,860
to past purchases.

780
00:23:58,040 --> 00:24:00,617
That's three hundred dollars that can't be

781
00:24:00,617 --> 00:24:02,519
used for this week's groceries,

782
00:24:02,519 --> 00:24:03,439
gas or savings.

783
00:24:03,789 --> 00:24:05,542
So what happens next?

784
00:24:05,722 --> 00:24:08,578
The person splits this week's groceries too,

785
00:24:08,578 --> 00:24:10,331
because the account is low.

786
00:24:10,511 --> 00:24:12,682
And now next month has another plan.

787
00:24:12,862 --> 00:24:14,557
This is how the loop forms.

788
00:24:14,737 --> 00:24:17,380
Past spending crowds out present needs,

789
00:24:17,380 --> 00:24:19,007
which creates new plans,

790
00:24:19,007 --> 00:24:20,972
which crowd out future needs.

791
00:24:21,152 --> 00:24:23,281
It's the paycheck to paycheck loop,

792
00:24:23,281 --> 00:24:25,227
just broken into smaller pieces.

793
00:24:25,577 --> 00:24:27,207
The way out is the same as

794
00:24:27,207 --> 00:24:28,085
any debt loop.

795
00:24:28,265 --> 00:24:29,558
Stop the new plans,

796
00:24:29,558 --> 00:24:31,192
let the old ones finish,

797
00:24:31,192 --> 00:24:33,439
and build even a small cushion so

798
00:24:33,439 --> 00:24:36,299
the next week doesn't depend on splitting.

799
00:24:36,479 --> 00:24:38,371
It might take one or two tight

800
00:24:38,371 --> 00:24:38,812
months.

801
00:24:38,992 --> 00:24:41,289
Then the money that went to installments

802
00:24:41,289 --> 00:24:42,150
is yours again.

803
00:24:42,500 --> 00:24:44,371
If what you love about buy now,

804
00:24:44,371 --> 00:24:46,422
pay later is spreading out a cost,

805
00:24:46,422 --> 00:24:48,293
there are better ways to do it.

806
00:24:48,473 --> 00:24:50,614
The best one is old fashioned:

807
00:24:50,614 --> 00:24:51,399
save first.

808
00:24:51,579 --> 00:24:53,631
Create a savings bucket for the thing

809
00:24:53,631 --> 00:24:55,184
you want and add to it every

810
00:24:55,184 --> 00:24:55,573
payday.

811
00:24:55,753 --> 00:24:56,861
When it's full,

812
00:24:56,861 --> 00:24:57,378
buy it.

813
00:24:57,558 --> 00:24:59,057
You get the same small,

814
00:24:59,057 --> 00:25:02,314
regular payments, just before the purchase instead

815
00:25:02,314 --> 00:25:03,096
of after it.

816
00:25:03,446 --> 00:25:05,837
Saving first has three advantages.

817
00:25:06,017 --> 00:25:08,267
No risk of late fees or credit

818
00:25:08,267 --> 00:25:08,792
damage.

819
00:25:08,972 --> 00:25:10,404
Time to change your mind,

820
00:25:10,404 --> 00:25:12,408
because many things you want today,

821
00:25:12,408 --> 00:25:14,011
you won't want in six weeks.

822
00:25:14,191 --> 00:25:16,228
And sometimes, while you save,

823
00:25:16,228 --> 00:25:17,315
the price drops,

824
00:25:17,315 --> 00:25:19,148
or a better option appears.

825
00:25:19,328 --> 00:25:22,531
Saving first turns impulse purchases into planned

826
00:25:22,531 --> 00:25:22,858
ones.

827
00:25:23,208 --> 00:25:25,160
For bigger necessary costs,

828
00:25:25,160 --> 00:25:26,896
plan with sinking funds,

829
00:25:26,896 --> 00:25:29,210
like we covered in other videos.

830
00:25:29,390 --> 00:25:31,931
A little each month for car repairs,

831
00:25:31,931 --> 00:25:34,684
holidays, appliances and medical costs.

832
00:25:34,864 --> 00:25:36,401
When the expense comes,

833
00:25:36,401 --> 00:25:37,604
it's already paid.

834
00:25:37,784 --> 00:25:39,753
And if you truly need to borrow,

835
00:25:39,753 --> 00:25:41,660
compare the total cost of a buy

836
00:25:41,660 --> 00:25:43,935
now, pay later plan with options like

837
00:25:43,935 --> 00:25:45,166
a credit union loan,

838
00:25:45,166 --> 00:25:47,196
and pick the cheapest one you can

839
00:25:47,196 --> 00:25:48,303
comfortably repay.

840
00:25:48,653 --> 00:25:50,499
Let's see two shoppers.

841
00:25:50,679 --> 00:25:52,125
Emma, twenty four,

842
00:25:52,125 --> 00:25:53,170
used buy now,

843
00:25:53,170 --> 00:25:55,741
pay later for almost everything.

844
00:25:55,921 --> 00:25:57,318
Shoes, a jacket,

845
00:25:57,318 --> 00:25:59,414
a phone, a weekend trip,

846
00:25:59,414 --> 00:26:01,772
even groceries a few times.

847
00:26:01,952 --> 00:26:03,473
Each plan seemed small.

848
00:26:03,653 --> 00:26:04,636
Then one month,

849
00:26:04,636 --> 00:26:06,405
her hours at work were cut.

850
00:26:06,585 --> 00:26:09,049
Suddenly she had about four hundred dollars

851
00:26:09,049 --> 00:26:11,169
of installments due within two weeks,

852
00:26:11,169 --> 00:26:12,889
and not enough in her account.

853
00:26:13,239 --> 00:26:14,451
One payment bounced,

854
00:26:14,451 --> 00:26:16,269
leading to a late fee from the

855
00:26:16,269 --> 00:26:18,450
lender and an overdraft fee from her

856
00:26:18,450 --> 00:26:18,753
bank.

857
00:26:18,933 --> 00:26:21,043
She started using her credit card to

858
00:26:21,043 --> 00:26:22,684
cover the next installments,

859
00:26:22,684 --> 00:26:23,914
which added interest.

860
00:26:24,094 --> 00:26:25,922
It took her about five months,

861
